  "id": "divide-in-two-steps",
  "name": "Divide in two easy steps",
  "rule": "Split the divisor into two small numbers: ÷6 = ÷2 then ÷3. ÷12 = ÷3 then ÷4. ÷15 = ÷3 then ÷5.",
  "example": "168 ÷ 12 = 168 ÷ 3 = 56, then 56 ÷ 4 = 14",
  "why": "12 is 3 × 4, so dividing by 12 is dividing by 3 and then by 4. Two small divisions are easier than one big one.",
